# Plan Comparison Table (`comparison-table`)

Plan comparison table: a highlight column glides to the plan you hover or focus (defaults to the recommended one), checkmarks draw in row by row when it scrolls into view, and the header stays sticky.

## What it should do
Build a plan comparison table: semantic table with a sticky header; the hovered/focused plan column gets a motion.span highlight with a shared layoutId behind its header plus tinted cells; boolean cells render a check path that draws (pathLength) with a row/column stagger once in view; false shows a muted minus.

## Project requirements
- React 19 + TypeScript, Tailwind CSS v4, shadcn/ui-style CSS variables (`background`, `foreground`, `muted`, `muted-foreground`, `border`, `card`, `primary`, `ring`). If the project lacks shadcn, set it up first (`npx shadcn@latest init`).
- Animation engine: **motion**.
- Install dependencies: `npm i motion lucide-react`
- Put the component at `components/kinetik/comparison-table.tsx`.
- `cn` lives at `lib/kinetik/utils.ts` (source below).
- Shared hooks go at `lib/kinetik/core.ts` (source below).
- Motion tokens go at `lib/kinetik/tokens.ts` (source below). Use tokens instead of magic numbers.

## Non-negotiables
- **Accessibility:** Real table with caption, column and row headers, colgroup headers; checks have 'Included' labels. Reduced motion: no drawing or gliding.
- **Performance:** One layoutId highlight; checks draw once.
- Respect `prefers-reduced-motion` (replace movement with opacity or an instant change).
- Animate only transform / opacity / filter / clip-path. No hard-coded theme colors — use CSS variables so it works in light and dark.

